	(text "Why analog instead of I2C (old TSL2591 breakout):\n - Old board ran I2C over a 6\" off-board harness; motor noise at comp + bus capacitance made it unreliable (Notion Blackbody v1.0.0, #array 10/5).\n - TSL2591 has a fixed address (0x29), so multiple sensors needed a mux/translator.\n - A silicon photodiode responds ~430-1100 nm, peak ~900 nm: same band the solar cells use (Aarav: 300-1100 nm, peak 800-950).\n - Short-circuit photocurrent is linear with irradiance; a current over shielded twisted pair is far less noise-sensitive than I2C.\n\nCandidate photodiode: Vishay BPW34 / BPW34S (7.5 mm2, 47 uA @ 1 mW/cm2, 950 nm). Calibrate one point against a reference meter (Kell: define 'peak sun').\nMounting: Ravi suggests the breakout on the underside of the top shell behind a window; wipe the window often.\nFault bits: IRRAD_DET high = breakout missing; Vout at rail = saturated; self-test mismatch = front end bad."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.830000000000005 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
